    "name": "os-lab-loop",
    "description": "The only improvement loop in the skill lab: orient from the improvement ledger, evals/results.tsv, references/program.md and open map debt, mutate one thing, call os-lab-scorer for every change (KEEP or DISCARD), then close with surveys, ledger update, metrics and memory promotion through os-lab-memory. Runs solo or as ORCHESTRATOR with INNER_AGENT and PEER_AGENT sessions sharing the kernel event bus. Use when the user says \"run the improvement loop\", \"run the autoresearch loop on\", \"optimize this skill for N iterations\", \"run an improvement cycle\", \"continuous improvement loop with KEEP or DISCARD\", \"ORCHESTRATOR and PEER_AGENT\", or \"close the loop\". DO NOT USE for a single KEEP/DISCARD check or one RED-GREEN-REFACTOR patch (os-lab-scorer), building the lab repo (os-lab-setup), planning (os-lab-planner), reviewing and porting results (os-lab-backport), run logs and charts (os-lab-log), or session memory alone (os-lab-memory).\n",
